{"book":{"id":"book-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen","slug":"on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen","title":"On British Islam: Religion, Law, and Everyday Practice in Shariʿa Councils","authors":[{"id":"person-john-r-bowen","name":"John R. Bowen"}],"publisherId":"publisher-princeton-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-princeton-university-press","isbn13":["9781400881055"],"subjects":["Society & Culture"],"topics":["Indigenous History","Gender & Feminism","Religion & Religious Movements","Law & Legal Change"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=On%20British%20Islam%3A%20Religion%2C%20Law%2C%20and%20Everyday%20Practice%20in%20Shari%CA%BFa%20Councils%20John%20R.%20Bowen","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=On%20British%20Islam%3A%20Religion%2C%20Law%2C%20and%20Everyday%20Practice%20in%20Shari%CA%BFa%20Councils%20John%20R.%20Bowen","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=On%20British%20Islam%3A%20Religion%2C%20Law%2C%20and%20Everyday%20Practice%20in%20Shari%CA%BFa%20Councils%20John%20R.%20Bowen","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=On%20British%20Islam%3A%20Religion%2C%20Law%2C%20and%20Everyday%20Practice%20in%20Shari%CA%BFa%20Councils%20John%20R.%20Bowen","publisher":"https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=xDDFCgAAQBAJ"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-laura-shannon-european-studies-laura-shannon-prize-2019-official-shortlist","source-google-books-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen","source-open-library-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen","source-cover-open-library-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen","source-imprint-normalization"],"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Social Science","sourceId":"source-google-books-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen"}],"publicationYear":2016,"pageCount":289,"summary":"On British Islam examines the history and everyday workings of Islamic institutions in Britain, with a focus on shariʿa councils. These councils concern themselves with religious matters, especially divorce. They have a higher profile in Britain than in other Western nations. Why? Taking a historical and ethnographic look at British Islam, John Bowen examines how Muslims have created distinctive religious institutions in Britain and how shariʿa councils interpret and apply Islamic law in a secular British context. Bowen focuses on three specific shariʿa councils: the oldest and most developed, in London; a Midlands community led by a Sufi saint and barrister; and a Birmingham-based council in which women play a leading role. Bowen shows that each of these councils represents a prolonged, unique experiment in meeting Muslims' needs in a Western country.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-on-british-islam-religion-law-and-everyday-practice-in-shari-a-councils-john-r-bowen.jpg","displaySummary":"On British Islam examines the history and everyday workings of Islamic institutions in Britain, with a focus on shariʿa councils. These councils concern themselves with religious matters, especially divorce. They have a higher profile in Britain than in other Western nations. Why? Taking a historical and ethnographic look at British Islam, John Bowen examines how Muslims have created distinctive religious institutions in Britain and how shariʿa councils interpret and apply Islamic law in a secular British context. Bowen focuses on three specific shariʿa councils: the oldest and most developed, in London; a Midlands community led by a Sufi saint and barrister; and a Birmingham-based council in which women play a leading role. Bowen shows that each of these councils represents a prolonged, unique experiment in meeting